Subject: Run the AOT unit on the threaded interpreter

What this does
  Lifts the restriction that an AOT unit needs the monolith. The threaded plus
  record build is now the default executor for an AOT build, and a unit runs
  there: `js_regvm_execute` already builds the activation record and enters the
  generated entry in every configuration.

Why we need it
  The shipping interpreter is the threaded plus record build, so an AOT unit
  that only runs on the monolith is not the unit that ships. The design makes
  this stage 2's second engine change (`E6`).

What it adds
  The `#error` that refused AOT outside the monolith is gone; the threaded
  default no longer excludes `QJS_AOT`; and a bound function is taken off the
  light path as well as the record path, so a call to it reaches the AOT entry
  instead of entering it as a light frame.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 1df072d..0d9fa01 100644
@@ -72,18 +72,15 @@
